# 4. Buttons in the slide

This example is a grid of 120 x 120 vertices whose positions are updated at each frame: either a ripple from
the center, or parallel waves. The surface is driven by buttons written in the text of the slide, outside the
frame of the demo. The current state is therefore visible in the slide, and the slide can also display a value
of the program.

