## What is new

- **Buttons in the slide,** in HTML only, with `slide-controls.js`: `data-demo-set` gives the settings to apply,
  `data-demo-value` shows a value live, and a button gets the class `on` while its settings are the current
  values of the demo.
- **A CGP scene of its own:** three files replace those of the template. `main.cpp` changes by one line
  (`slide::parse(argc, argv)`); the parameters are declared in `scene.cpp`.
- **The ImGui window of the template** is hidden in a slide (the page has its panel), unless `?gui=1`.

<div class="callout warn"><div class="callout-title">A trap of the web: the wireframe</div>

`draw_wireframe()` of CGP uses `glPolygonMode`, which WebGL does not have: on the web it draws nothing, without
an error. The wireframe here is a `curve_drawable` of segments (`GL_LINES`), drawn the same way on the desktop
and on the web. The browser test of the example caught it: the image did not change when the wireframe was
turned on.

</div>

## The files

```
examples/c3-cgp-waving-surface/
  src/main.cpp       the main() of the template, plus slide::parse
  src/scene.hpp      the parameters of the wave
  src/scene.cpp      the scene: the grid, the wave, the wireframe, the declared parameters
  slides.html        the slide, with its buttons
  demo.json          the browser test of the example
```

